Interpretation:
  An edge q -> c CAN HAVE F_3 = square iff p-adically compatible at ALL primes.
  The remaining obstruction (after p-adic) is that F_3 must NOT have a 'hidden'
  prime obstruction (i.e., square at infinity and at all p, by Hasse principle).
  Since F_3 is positive and the primes 2,3,5,7,11 cover the small-prime
  obstructions, all-5-compatible means F_3 is *probably* square — but we
  test issquare(F_3) directly which is the definitive test.
